# Git Commit Identity

All commits in this repository must use **PinkPurpleRed** as the author and committer name.

## Required identity

- **Name:** `PinkPurpleRed`
- **Never use:** `Evelyn`, `CursorAgent`, `Cursor`, or any other author name
- **Never add** `Co-authored-by` trailers (especially `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>`)

## When creating commits

Before committing, ensure the local repo identity is set:

```bash
git config --local user.name "PinkPurpleRed"
```

If local config is missing or wrong, set it before `git commit`. You may also pass identity explicitly:

```bash
GIT_AUTHOR_NAME="PinkPurpleRed" GIT_COMMITTER_NAME="PinkPurpleRed" git commit ...
```

## When rewriting history

If commits were made with the wrong author or co-author trailers, rewrite them before pushing. Do not leave Evelyn, CursorAgent, or Cursor co-author lines in commit history or contributor attribution.
